{\"B\": 2, \"S\": 4096}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.0255}, \"bb262a64\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 2048}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.1842}}, \"geomean_speedup\": 1.0809, \"all_correct\": true, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"decision_reason\": \"All 5 workloads correct; baseline geomean 1.0809x. WL3 (M=8192, B=32,S=256) at 0.8887x is the weak point: conservative 64x64x32 tile underperforms cuBLAS at large M, confirming prediction P1 (GEMM tuning highest leverage). Set as current best-correct.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 1, \"skill_usage\": \"none (KernelWiki N/A for sm_80; profiler disallowed)\"}\n{\"candidate_id\": \"c002\", \"parent\": \"c001\", \"source_sha256\": \"e3125cb9dd66a438a90eac8a6e9f008c2defec7da35c9689fa2815d304eef8b2\", \"hypothesis\": \"Phase B (P1): c001's fixed 64x64x32 GEMM tile underperforms cuBLAS at large M (WL3 0.889x). Add @triton.autotune over a curated Ampere bf16 tile menu on the shared GEMM kernel (used by both K1 and K3), keyed on (M,N,K). All feedback shapes are mask-free (M mult 256, N mult 256, K mult 128). Expect the single largest geomean jump, especially recovering WL3 to >=1x.\", \"change_vs_parent\": \"Added @triton.autotune (11 configs: BLOCK_M/N in {64,128,256}, BLOCK_K in {32,64}, GROUP_M=8, stages 3-4, warps 4-8) on _gemm_bias_kernel keyed on (M,N,K); removed fixed per-call BLOCK/warps/stages; grid lambdas now read META['BLOCK_M/N']. K2 fused conv kernel and all numerics unchanged.\", \"validation\": {\"analytical_checks\": [\"kernel math identical to c001 (only tile-selection policy changed)\", \"all feedback shapes divide every tile evenly -> mask-free correctness preserved\", \"fp32 accum + bf16 store unchanged\", \"K2 unchanged\"], \"expected_correct\": true}, \"results\": {\"b0a9e3f0\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 1024}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.6626}, \"8b678b13\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 4, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.6746}, \"58e3ac47\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 32, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3147}, \"6033fd0f\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 4096}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3296}, \"bb262a64\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 2048}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.4000}}, \"geomean_speedup\": 1.4678, \"all_correct\": true, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"decision_reason\": \"All 5 correct; geomean 1.0809x -> 1.4678x (+35.8%), the single largest jump so far, confirming prediction P1 (GEMMs dominate, tile policy is the primary lever). WL3 recovered from 0.889x to 1.315x. New current best-correct. Next: Phase C (fuse/tile the memory-bound K2) since GEMM tuning is largely captured; small-M cases (WL1/2 at ~1.66x) now lead, large-M (WL3/4 ~1.32x) lag -> remaining headroom is intermediate-traffic + launch overhead reduction.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 2, \"skill_usage\": \"none (KernelWiki N/A for sm_80; profiler disallowed)\"}\n{\"candidate_id\": \"c003\", \"parent\": \"c002\", \"source_sha256\": \"b19cb64757825d4656a1eeb992bac072abcd38e7f2eaac46adff124f835bab3b\", \"hypothesis\": \"Phase C (P2): K2 (fused gating+causal-conv+gating) is memory-bound and was left at a fixed conservative 64x64/warps=4 tile in c001/c002. Add @triton.autotune over a K2 launch-config menu (BLOCK_M in {16,32,64,128}, BLOCK_H in {64,128,256}, num_warps {4,8}) keyed on (M,S,H), favoring large coalesced BLOCK_H along the contiguous H axis. Kernel math byte-for-byte identical to c002 (only launch policy tuned); baseline 64x64/w4 retained so autotune picks min over a superset. Expect a small gain (draft P2: middle is minor vs GEMMs), most visible on large-M WL3/WL4 where K2 traffic is largest.\", \"change_vs_parent\": \"Added @triton.autotune (9 configs) on _fused_conv_kernel keyed on (M,S,H); removed fixed _BM2/_BH2=64 launch; grid2 now reads META['BLOCK_M','BLOCK_H']. GEMM kernel, its autotune menu, and all numerics unchanged.\", \"validation\": {\"analytical_checks\": [\"K2 math identical to c002 (only tile-selection policy changed)\", \"per-row guard s=offs_m%S; valid=s>=d handles causal pad + batch boundary for ANY (BLOCK_M,BLOCK_H) incl. tiles spanning batches\", \"every tensor dim masked (m_mask,h_mask) -> M/H overhang safe\", \"acc regs/thread = BLOCK_M*BLOCK_H/(32*num_warps) <= 64 -> no spills\", \"GEMM path unchanged -> GEMM correctness preserved\"], \"expected_correct\": true}, \"results\": {\"b0a9e3f0\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 1024}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.6554}, \"8b678b13\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 4, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.6681}, \"58e3ac47\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 32, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3336}, \"6033fd0f\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 4096}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3419}, \"bb262a64\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 2048}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.4007}}, \"geomean_speedup\": 1.4724, \"all_correct\": true, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"decision_reason\": \"All 5 correct; geomean 1.4678x -> 1.4724x (+0.31%). Confirms prediction P2: the memory-bound middle is minor vs the GEMMs, so tuning K2 yields only a small gain. Gain concentrated on large-M cases WL3 (1.3147->1.3336) and WL4 (1.3296->1.3419) where K2 traffic is largest, as predicted; small-M WL1/WL2 dipped ~0.4-0.6% (autotune timing noise, within measurement variance) and WL5 flat. New current best-correct (1.4724x >= 1.4678x). Remaining headroom is now almost entirely in the GEMMs (which dominate) and in eliminating the intermediate BCx(M,3H)/y(M,H) write+read via fusion (F1: fold input gating into GEMM1 epilogue).\", \"cumulative_evals\": 3, \"skill_usage\": \"none (KernelWiki N/A for sm_80; profiler disallowed)\"}\n{\"candidate_id\": \"c004\", \"parent\": \"c003\", \"source_sha256\": \"d14d02a6e928fd189b3900df986158dd593a98185ad51af19836ab412f46c528\", \"hypothesis\": \"Phase B refine: c003's large-M cases (WL3/WL4 ~1.33x) lag small-M (~1.66x). Expand the GEMM @triton.autotune menu from 11 to 18 configs (superset: all c003 configs + 7 A800-oriented large-M tiles: s5 deep pipelines, high-BLOCK_M 256x64, GROUP_M=16 L2-reuse, extra warp/shape variety). GEMM kernel body + all numerics byte-for-byte identical to c003; K2 unchanged. Expected geomean >= c003 since autotune picks min over a superset.\", \"change_vs_parent\": \"Added 7 configs to _gemm_configs() (18 total, strict superset of c003's 11). No kernel-body or numeric change; K2 unchanged.\", \"validation\": {\"analytical_checks\": [\"GEMM kernel math identical to c003 (only tile menu grew)\", \"all added tiles mask-free on M mult 256 / N mult 256 / K mult 128\", \"smem <= ~147KB and regs <= 128/thread for every added tile\"], \"expected_correct\": true}, \"results\": {\"6033fd0f\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 4096}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3297}, \"36e77f89\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 1879}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3733}, \"121c8e28\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 16, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.4206}, \"1408082c\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 2048}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.4015}, \"bb262a64\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 2048}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3826}, \"66fd2ad8\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, \"58e3ac47\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 32, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3211}, \"0a859b3a\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 4096}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.4058}, \"3ac091d6\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 4, \"S\": 512}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3759}, \"dcc98535\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 128}, \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, \"d9432839\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 8, \"S\": 997}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3035}, \"01719394\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 8192}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3549}, \"b0a9e3f0\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 1024}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3409}, \"b662596d\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 4, \"S\": 541}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3668}, \"1979d4cb\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 1024}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3822}, \"8b678b13\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 4, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3586}}, \"geomean_speedup\": 1.3651, \"all_correct\": false, \"decision\": \"reject\", \"decision_reason\": \"ENVIRONMENT CHANGE DISCOVERED: the feedback stage now runs 16 workloads (was 5). c004 is INVALID: 14/16 passed; 2 INCORRECT_NUMERICAL on the two smallest-M cases 66fd2ad8 (B1,S256,M=256) and dcc98535 (B2,S128,M=256), both max_abs=0.0625 with <99% match. Since c004's GEMM math is byte-for-byte identical to c003, the menu expansion did NOT cause this; it is a pre-existing numerical edge case exposed by the newly-added tight-tolerance small-M workloads. Root cause (draft s2.3/s4.2): our K2 keeps the middle in fp32, but the reference rounds Bx, conv_out, and y to bf16 at each intermediate step; on tight-atol small problems the fp32-vs-bf16 divergence pushes >1% of elements out of tolerance. Note: c003/c002/c001 were only ever validated on the old 5-workload set, so no candidate is yet known-valid on the 16-set. Next: c005 = c003 base (revert c004's menu to isolate the fix) + mirror the reference's intermediate bf16 roundings in K2 (round Bx before conv, conv_out before the output gate).\", \"cumulative_evals\": 4, \"skill_usage\": \"none (KernelWiki N/A for sm_80; profiler disallowed)\"}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"candidate_id\": \"c002\", \"parent\": \"c001\", \"source_sha256\": \"e3125cb9dd66a438a90eac8a6e9f008c2defec7da35c9689fa2815d304eef8b2\", \"hypothesis\": \"Phase B (P1): c001's fixed 64x64x32 GEMM tile underperforms cuBLAS at large M (WL3 0.889x). Add @triton.autotune over a curated Ampere bf16 tile menu on the shared GEMM kernel (used by both K1 and K3), keyed on (M,N,K). All feedback shapes are mask-free (M mult 256, N mult 256, K mult 128). Expect the single largest geomean jump, especially recovering WL3 to >=1x.\", \"change_vs_parent\": \"Added @triton.autotune (11 configs: BLOCK_M/N in {64,