6% (autotune timing noise, within measurement variance) and WL5 flat. New current best-correct (1.4724x >= 1.4678x). Remaining headroom is now almost entirely in the GEMMs (which dominate) and in eliminating the intermediate BCx(M,3H)/y(M,H) write+read via fusion (F1: fold input gating into GEMM1 epilogue).\", \"cumulative_evals\": 3, \"skill_usage\": \"none (KernelWiki N/A for sm_80; profiler disallowed)\"}"," {\"candidate_id\": \"c004\", \"parent\": \"c003\", \"source_sha256\": \"d14d02a6e928fd189b3900df986158dd593a98185ad51af19836ab412f46c528\", \"hypothesis\": \"Phase B refine: c003's large-M cases (WL3/WL4 ~1.33x) lag small-M (~1.66x). Expand the GEMM @triton.autotune menu from 11 to 18 configs (superset: all c003 configs + 7 A800-oriented large-M tiles: s5 deep pipelines, high-BLOCK_M 256x64, GROUP_M=16 L2-reuse, extra warp/shape variety). GEMM kernel body + all numerics byte-for-byte identical to c003; K2 unchanged. Expected geomean >= c003 since autotune picks min over a superset.\", \"change_vs_parent\": \"Added 7 configs to _gemm_configs() (18 total, strict superset of c003's 11). No kernel-body or numeric change; K2 unchanged.\", \"validation\": {\"analytical_checks\": [\"GEMM kernel math identical to c003 (only tile menu grew)\", \"all added tiles mask-free on M mult 256 / N mult 256 / K mult 128\", \"smem <= ~147KB and regs <= 128/thread for every added tile\"], \"expected_correct\": true}, \"results\": {\"6033fd0f\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 4096}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3297}, \"36e77f89\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 1879}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3733}, \"121c8e28\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 16, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.4206}, \"1408082c\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 2048}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.4015}, \"bb262a64\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 2048}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3826}, \"66fd2ad8\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, \"58e3ac47\": {