ative_evals\": 4, \"skill_usage\": \"none (KernelWiki N/A for sm_80; profiler disallowed)\"}","+{\"candidate_id\": \"c005\", \"parent\": \"c003\", \"source_sha256\": \"755e3f87d6a2ceca8af04f9a22206b1673e777b831e9616764ca1c7364c68ef8\", \"hypothesis\": \"Correctness repair for the newly-discovered 16-workload feedback set. c004 failed the two smallest-M cases (66fd2ad8 B1/S256, dcc98535 B2/S128; both M=256, INCORRECT_NUMERICAL) because our K2 kept the middle in fp32 while the reference materializes Bx/conv_out/y in bf16 at each stage (draft s2.3/s4.2). Fix: (1) revert GEMM menu to c003's 11 configs (isolate the change), (2) mirror the reference's intermediate bf16 roundings in K2: round Bx=(Bgate*Xproj) to bf16 before the 4-tap fp32 conv accumulation, and round conv_out=(acc+conv_bias) to bf16 before the output gate. Expect all 16 valid; small perf cost from extra casts.\", \"change_vs_parent\": \"vs c003: added two bf16-round steps inside _fused_conv_kernel (bx before conv accum; conv_out before output gate). GEMM menu identical to c003 (reverts c004's 7 extra configs). K2 autotune menu + all launch plumbing unchanged.\", \"validation\": {\"analytical_checks\": [\"conv accum still fp32 over 4 taps (matches cuDNN fp32-accum-then-round)\", \"bf16 rounds placed exactly where reference materializes bf16 tensors (Bx, conv_out)\", \"GEMM path byte-for-byte c003\", \"per-row causal+batch guard unchanged -> correctness for any tile\", \"output gate y=Cgate*conv_out stored bf16 unchanged\"], \"expected_correct\": true}, \"results\": {\"6033fd0f\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 4096}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3269}, \"36e77f89\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 1879}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3826}, \"121c8e28\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 16, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.4231}, \"1408082c\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 2048}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.4038}, \"bb262a64\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 2048}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3949}, \"66fd2ad8\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.4124}, \"58e3ac47\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 32, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3589}, \"0a859b3a\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 4096}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.4076}, \"3ac091d6\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 4, \"S\": 512}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3780}, \"dcc98535\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 128}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.4124}, \"d9432839\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 8, \"S\": 997}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3063}, \"01719394\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 8192}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3610}, \"b0a9e3f0\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 1024}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3483}, \"b662596d\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 4, \"S\": 541}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3745}, \"1979d4cb\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 1024}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3848}, \"8b678b13\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 4, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3663}}, \"geomean_speedup\": 1.3772, \"all_correct\": true, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"decision_reason\": \"VALID on all 16/16 workloads; geomean 1.3772x. The bf16-round lever fixed the two small-M failures exactly as predicted (66fd2ad8 and dcc98535 now pass at 1.4124x). This is the FIRST candidate known-valid on the true 16-workload feedback set, so it becomes the new baseline / current best-correct (prior c001-c003 were only validated on the old 5-set and are not comparable). Perf profile: small-M cases lead (~1.40-1.42x), large-M/large-S lag (~1.31-1.36x), matching the earlier GEMM-bound picture. Next: resume perf tuning now measured against the 16-set geomean -- re-introduce the large-M GEMM tiles (the safe subset of c004's additions, now that correctness is decoupled) as c006, since GEMMs still dominate and large-M cases (d9432839 1.306x, 6033fd0f 1.327x) are the laggards.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 5, \"skill_usage\": \"none (KernelWiki N/A for sm_80; profiler disallowed)\"}"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
