 B on the 16-set):** GEMMs still dominate and the\n  laggards are the large-M/large-S cases. Re-introduce the safe subset of c004's large-M GEMM\n  tiles (deeper `s5` pipelines at BLOCK_K=32, high-BLOCK_M `256×64`, `GROUP_M=16` for L2 reuse\n  at large M) on top of c005's now-correct numerics. Correctness is decoupled (menu change\n  cannot affect numerics — all shapes still mask-free, incl. new M values: M=256,512,…,8192\n  all mult. 256? NOTE new shapes have odd S like 997,1879,541 -> M=B*S may NOT be mult of 256\n  (e.g. B8*S997=7976, B4*S541=2164, B2*S1879=3758). Verify: GEMM kernel masks M via\n  `m_mask = offs_m < M`, so ragged M is already handled — c005 passed these, confirming the\n  mask path is correct. Any tile is therefore safe.) Expected: lift the large-M laggards,\n  small 16-set geomean gain. Keep on improvement."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":112894,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ebfc772f-ed07-4815-a18f-b2c61ed9c734","uuid":"8672609d-215a-43a9-b255-c10594ba88cb","timestamp":"2026-09-20T04:40:39.514Z"}
